// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/site-in-two-languages.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeSiteInTwoLanguages(path: "/recipes/site-in-two-languages", title: "Publish a page in each language — Recipes", description: "Have search engines find each language: write each page once per language at its own address, with lang: and translates: joining them.") {
    RecipeShell("Publish a page in each language", summary: "Have a search engine find your site in each of its languages. `t()` and `setLocale` translate a page in the browser, at one address, and a search engine indexes what that address's HTML says, which is the default locale. A site that wants each language found writes each page once per language, at an address of its own, and says how the pages are joined.  This site is written in Arabic, with its home page in English at `/en`:", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Keep writes made offline", to: "/recipes/keep-writes-made-offline"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Make a site work offline", to: "/recipes/work-offline"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Offer a new version", to: "/recipes/offer-a-new-version")], source: "md-docs/recipes/site-in-two-languages.md", how: true, hasVariations: false) {
        code {
            CodeBlock(#"page Home(path: "/", title: "منذر عمر", description: "مهندس خلفيات.") {
    Heading("مرحباً").h1
}

page HomeEn(path: "/en", title: "Monzer Omer", description: "Engineer.",
            lang: "en", translates: Home) {
    Heading("Hello").h1
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        Markdown("- **`lang:`** is the language the page is written in. A page without one is in the site's (`meta.lang`, or `default_locale`). The page is written `<html lang=\"en\">`, with `dir=\"rtl\"` for a language written right to left, and its `og:locale` and its JSON-LD's `inLanguage` say the same. The router sets `lang` and `dir` on `<html>` when it shows the page, and puts back the site's (or the locale the reader chose) on a page without one.\n- **`translates:`** names the page this one is a translation of. Pages joined this way — `HomeFr` may translate `Home` too — each list all of them as `hreflang` alternates, at their own addresses and canonical to themselves, with `x-default` for the one in the site's language, and each names the others' languages as `og:locale:alternate`.\n- **A `:param` page's translation is matched by its parameters:** `/en/posts/:slug` for `/posts/:slug`, filled with the same `slug`.\n\nA `translates:` that names no page, or two translations of one page in one language, is `R05`.")

    }
}
